<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Sinfonia sacra (Andrzej Panufnik)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1963</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bogurodzica (Wojciech Kilar), for choir and orchestra</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1975</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphony No. 6 &quot;Polish&quot; (Krzysztof Meyer)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1982</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Symphony No. 1 (Henryk Górecki)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1959</span><span class="sg-chain-h">its opening used as a motto</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Songs of Joy and Rhythm (Henryk Górecki, 1960 version)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1960</span><span class="sg-chain-h">its opening used as a motto</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Harpsichord Concerto, op. 40 (Henryk Górecki)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1980</span><span class="sg-chain-h">its opening used as a motto in the first movement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Miserere, op. 44 (Henryk Górecki)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1981</span><span class="sg-chain-h">its opening used as a motto</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bogurodzica (Chłopomania, from Ludomania)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2008</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bogurodzica (Anna Witczak Czerniawska &amp; Maleo Reggae Rockers feat. Mazzoll)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2015</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Theotokos (Greek title of Mary)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">its name is a calque of the Greek term</span></li></ul></section>
